cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use urdf-usd-bridge in work you publish, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: "urdf-usd-bridge: a stability layer and cross-backend validator for URDF-derived OpenUSD robot assets"
abstract: >-
  Robot descriptions converted from URDF to OpenUSD are kinematically faithful
  but dynamically underdetermined: they carry no drive gains, no rotor inertia,
  sometimes no inertia tensor, and joints that the converter welded shut
  because the source URDF omitted a limit element. Each physics backend fills
  those gaps with its own defaults, so one asset simulates as three different
  robots. urdf-usd-bridge closes the gaps explicitly. It reports, per
  namespace, what physics data an asset actually carries; derives PD gains,
  armature and inertia tensors from the robot's own geometry; restores joint
  limits where the evidence is unambiguous and refuses to guess where it is
  not; and authors the result as non-destructive USD overlay layers in each
  backend's own unit convention, leaving the input file untouched. It ships a
  cross-backend simulation harness that drives PhysX, Newton and MuJoCo Warp
  from a single interpreter, so every tuning constant is either measured or
  explicitly labelled unmeasured. Across 14 robots and 3 backends, repair
  improved hold-pose drift in 35 of 84 cells and worsened it in none, 19 runs
  that diverged on converter output converged after repair, and cross-backend
  agreement improved from 7.9e-2 to 7.6e-5 radians. The work also produced
  three reproducible defect reports against its own dependencies.
type: software
